{"id": "EUVD-2026-103847", "enisaUuid": "b679217a-e209-3ee4-88cd-a30eaedd6a6a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nUSB: dwc2: shut down wakeup timer before freeing HCD state\n\ndwc2_wakeup_detected() accesses the DWC2 host state and can rearm the\nwakeup timer.  dwc2_hcd_free() currently deletes the timer only after\nfreeing host-owned state, and timer_delete() does not synchronize a\ncallback or prevent it from being queued again.\n\nStop and shut down the timer in dwc2_hcd_release(), before the HCD\nresources are freed.  This covers both the HCD initialization error path\nand normal HCD removal.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82cc242da6d621752718929e6a2fa6f9554ebffe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/441be312fce927443eae2821f502344d953c38bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4333174ea52c863a50bb3e0a4726bf9f7cdf7524", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79ba37dd38a321cb32a79332a3e3c68dd334dca9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd772af9512cdecb83de34a461801533828e77fd"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g24x-rpv9-j8mw", "CVE-2026-98762"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06098d56-c08e-3f54-89fe-f73c6ec9b25a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7359d482eb4d3967cc8be354405ae6be6eaf732c <4333174ea52c863a50bb3e0a4726bf9f7cdf7524"}, {"id": "0a05d6c2-0696-355e-a716-7cb6705a768f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "13dcff33-e7a8-30ad-b247-eece48448c42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "43504d49-cc36-397e-bb6a-5a19ead6ca91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4dae7445-97c1-354a-a27f-ede0cfb4bbc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}